# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — Industrial Digital Twin Workspace
# Authoritative scope: matches `gitignored` annotations in docs/runtime_policy.md
# §1.1 and docs/storage_policy.md §2.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Workspace runtime/output directories (per docs) -------------------------
# Per docs/runtime_policy.md §1.1: logs/, datasets/, outputs/ are gitignored.
# Per docs/storage_policy.md §2:    cache/ is gitignored (13th canonical dir).
logs/
datasets/
outputs/
cache/

# Keep the 4 directories above tracked-but-empty by adding a .gitkeep
# inside each one (not done by this .gitignore). If empty-dir tracking
# becomes important, add a `!logs/.gitkeep` line per directory.

# ---- Python bytecode + virtual envs -----------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/

# Editable installs and build artifacts
build/
dist/
*.egg
pip-wheel-metadata/

# ---- IDE / editor cruft ------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Profile-specific runtime artefacts (must never leak in) -----------------
# Isaac Sim writes here when invoked from this workspace.
**/.nvidia-omniverse/
**/omni.replicator_out/

# Backup files
*~
*.bak
*.orig

# ---- NVIDIA Nsight / streaming capture files --------------------------------
# NvStreamer-*.etli are GPU-trace captures written to the workspace root by the
# Isaac Sim WebRTC streaming session. Large binary artifacts, never
# replay-authoritative; must not be committed.
*.etli

# ---- Local secrets / environment overrides -----------------------------------
# Generally none expected, but kept conservative.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
